/E (Excavation is one of the most hazardous construction activities, essential for foundations, utility lines, and water/sewer systems. It includes any man-made cut, trench, or depression in the earth formed by removal of soil. The major risks include cave-ins, contact with utility lines, and hazardous atmospheres. Awareness, planning, and safety management are critical.)
